    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#historyNote": [
      {
        "@value": "AGS 4.1: Group Rule Added - • MOND_RDNG should generally be numeric data. A text form shall only be used by addition of a prefixing operator to denote greater than or less than conditions i.e. >200 when readings are above the reporting limit of the testing equipment. • Where a reading has no unit, the MOND_UNIT data shall be set to 'UNITLESS'. • Units included in MOND_UNIT shall be fully defined in the UNIT group (Rule 15). • MOND_UNIT data type shall not be changed from PU type.\nAGS 4.1: Headings Updated - MOND_DIS description updated to 'Initial distance of monitoring point from LOCA_ID datum' from 'Initial distance of monitoring point from LOCA_ID'"
      }
    ],
